          "secNumber": "2.15",
          "heading": "Unit 2 Review and Methodological Synthesis",
          "content": "In Unit 2, we examined dimension reduction methodologies for high-dimensional and massive datasets. We analyzed the breakdown of classical PCA consistency in the Marchenko-Pastur regime ($p/n \\to \\gamma$), proving that noise eigenvalues disperse across $[\\sigma^2(1-\\sqrt{\\gamma})^2, \\sigma^2(1+\\sqrt{\\gamma})^2]$. We formulated the BBP phase transition, showing that true signal eigenvalues must exceed $1 + \\sqrt{\\gamma}$ to emerge from the noise bulk. We examined the Tracy-Widom $F_1$ law governing the fluctuation of the leading sample eigenvalue. We developed Randomized SVD via the Halko-Martinsson-Tropp algorithm, proving near-optimal low-rank reconstruction in $O(n p \\log k)$ operations. We detailed non-linear manifold learning via t-SNE (Kullback-Leibler divergence with Student-$t$ kernels) and UMAP (fuzzy simplicial sets and cross-entropy optimization). Finally, we surveyed Sparse PCA, Random Fourier Features for kernel scaling, Robust PCA via Principal Component Pursuit, and Non-Negative Matrix Factorization.",
